15. BROADER PRODUCER OBSERVABILITY / ECONOMICS DESIGN ALREADY AGREED
======================================================================

Producer history retention is intended to distinguish two classes.

A. NEVER CREATED EXPOSURE

Examples:

decision_failed
decision_blocked
produced only
entry_failed
pending → cancelled
rejected
expired
cleanup_cancelled
etc.

Retention anchor:

ProducerAttempt.CreatedAt

Prune after the configured retention window, currently 24h.

B. CREATED EXPOSURE

If filled or partially filled resulted in committed exposure:

DO NOT prune merely because ProducerAttempt.CreatedAt is older than 24h.

Use entry OrderID to associate the attempt with the resulting position/trade.

If position remains OPEN:

keep ProducerAttempt regardless of age.

If position EXITED:

retention anchor becomes exit.Time

and prune after exit.Time is older than 24h.

At prune time we intend to update compact persistent aggregate producer economics.

Desired per-producer aggregate includes:

attempts
fills
cancelled attempts
failed attempts

open positions
closed positions

wins
losses
win rate

gross/net realized PnL as appropriate to existing exit semantics

average PnL per trade

average individual trade percentage return

The desired return metric is:

average of each individual trades percentage return

NOT:

NetPnL / total deployed capital

because sizing is not fundamentally capital-based in this bot and available spare may reduce proposed size or block an entry.

For each closed trade conceptually:

tradeReturnPct =
    (realizedPnLUSD / entryOpenNotionalUSD) * 100

Maintain a running sum:

SumTradeReturnPct

and derive:

AverageReturnPct =
    SumTradeReturnPct /
    ClosedPositions

Existing PNLUSD is intended to be fee-aware, so do not automatically double-count fees by subtracting them again.

We also decided NOT to maintain a growing ProcessedExits dedupe map for this design. Aggregate economics are intended to be updated once when the corresponding attempt becomes eligible for pruning.

Do not work on this economics/pruning phase yet unless the Decision/wrapper lifecycle work is complete.

